00:11:23.989 --> 00:11:26.632
if your album, Tha Carter III,

00:11:26.632 --> 00:11:31.546
was the biggest-selling
album of the year in 2008?

00:11:31.546 --> 00:11:34.621
- Isn't it something that
I would remember that?

00:11:34.621 --> 00:11:36.368
- [Pete] Yes.

00:11:36.368 --> 00:11:40.287
- Isn't that a personal
opinion-type question?

00:11:40.287 --> 00:11:44.327
Because I would be actually
answering a question to

00:11:44.327 --> 00:11:46.859
isn't it something, that's my question?

00:11:46.859 --> 00:11:47.949
Isn't it something?

00:11:47.949 --> 00:11:49.900
- [Pete] That you would remember.

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:51.203
- Isn't it something?

00:11:51.203 --> 00:11:53.262
That's the question I have
to answer, your Honor?

00:11:53.262 --> 00:11:55.651
Isn't it something?

00:11:55.651 --> 00:11:57.359
- [Judge] Do the best to try to answer it.

00:11:57.359 --> 00:11:59.244
(laughing)

00:11:59.244 --> 00:12:02.506
- Yeah, it's something out of your ass.

00:12:02.506 --> 00:12:04.510
That's my answer.

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:06.823
Yeah, it is something out of your ass.

00:12:06.823 --> 00:12:09.082
- [Pete] Have you ever
hired a photographer

00:12:09.082 --> 00:12:10.999
to photograph an event?

00:12:12.281 --> 00:12:13.641
- Have I ever hired a photographer

00:12:13.641 --> 00:12:14.917
to photograph an event?

00:12:14.917 --> 00:12:15.882
Sorry sir, no.

00:12:15.882 --> 00:12:16.945
I'm a superstar.

00:12:16.945 --> 00:12:20.393
People hire them themselves
to photograph me.

00:12:20.393 --> 00:12:22.724
We don't hire them.

00:12:22.724 --> 00:12:26.779
- [Pete] How would you describe
your image in the media?

00:12:26.779 --> 00:12:29.028
- How would I describe
my image in the media?

00:12:29.028 --> 00:12:29.861
- [Pete] Yes.

00:12:29.861 --> 00:12:31.944
- I wouldn't describe it.

00:12:33.584 --> 00:12:36.035
- [Pete] Well how would you
describe it if you had to?

00:12:36.035 --> 00:12:37.186
- I don't have to.

00:12:37.186 --> 00:12:40.142
- [Pete] Well what image are
you portraying in the media?

00:12:40.142 --> 00:12:41.518
- I don't portray anything.

00:12:41.518 --> 00:12:42.818
I am who I am,

00:12:42.818 --> 00:12:45.082
and you guys portray what you get.

00:12:45.082 --> 00:12:46.203
- [Pete] Who are you?

00:12:46.203 --> 00:12:47.036
Who's the real?

00:12:47.036 --> 00:12:49.201
- I am Dwayne Michael Carter, Jr.

00:12:49.201 --> 00:12:50.085
- [Pete] Okay.

00:12:50.085 --> 00:12:50.918
Do you

00:12:52.396 --> 00:12:54.529
like to portray yourself as--

00:12:54.529 --> 00:12:55.878
- I just answered that and said that

00:12:55.878 --> 00:12:59.160
I don't like to portray myself as nobody.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:02.106
I completely be Dwayne Michael Carter, Jr.

00:13:02.106 --> 00:13:04.116
I don't portray myself as anything.

00:13:04.116 --> 00:13:05.938
An image is self-described.

00:13:05.938 --> 00:13:06.771
- [Pete] Well you have to wait until

00:13:06.771 --> 00:13:07.835
I'm done with the question.

00:13:07.835 --> 00:13:09.451
- I don't have to wait until anything.

00:13:09.451 --> 00:13:11.284
Honestly, I mean,

00:13:11.284 --> 00:13:13.311
this guy right here may
tell me that I have to wait.

00:13:13.311 --> 00:13:15.421
But personally, I don't
have to do nothing.

00:13:15.421 --> 00:13:16.891
Tonight say hell yeah.

00:13:16.891 --> 00:13:18.746
- [Crowd] Hell yeah.

00:13:18.746 --> 00:13:21.023
(crowd cheering)

00:13:21.023 --> 00:13:22.773
- Hold on one second.

00:13:23.921 --> 00:13:27.698
Hold on one second, one
second, one second, one second.

00:13:27.698 --> 00:13:30.798
Don't throw no ice at me, homie.

00:13:30.798 --> 00:13:31.931
Don't throw no ice at me,

00:13:31.931 --> 00:13:36.242
because listen, listen,
not none of these security,

00:13:36.242 --> 00:13:38.963
none of these niggas around me.

00:13:38.963 --> 00:13:41.256
It'll be me that you up.

00:13:41.256 --> 00:13:42.879
- Tell me how did you guys connect,

00:13:42.879 --> 00:13:43.807
because you all are friends

00:13:43.807 --> 00:13:45.629
and he's been a big influence on.

00:13:45.629 --> 00:13:47.045
You know Lil Wayne and I are like this.

00:13:47.045 --> 00:13:48.715
- I know, I know that's your dawg.

00:13:48.715 --> 00:13:50.274
- Yeah, that's my dawg.

00:13:50.274 --> 00:13:51.552
(laughing)

00:13:51.552 --> 00:13:53.631
He kept saying to me, "I'm
a gangsta, Ms. Katie."

00:13:53.631 --> 00:13:55.125
- I remember, I remember the interview.

00:13:55.125 --> 00:13:55.958
I watched it.

00:13:55.958 --> 00:13:56.791
It was great.

00:13:56.791 --> 00:13:59.699
- But how did you guys
get to know each other?

00:13:59.699 --> 00:14:02.845
- We were introduced through
another gentleman from Houston.

00:14:02.845 --> 00:14:04.762
His name is Jas Prince.

00:14:05.895 --> 00:14:10.685
He found me on Myspace and
loved my music on Myspace,

00:14:10.685 --> 00:14:13.714
and he was like, "Man, I know Lil Wayne

00:14:13.714 --> 00:14:15.243
"and I'm going to play
him your music one day,"

00:14:15.243 --> 00:14:18.778
and I was just like (scoffs)
yeah right, you know.

00:14:18.778 --> 00:14:20.165
I didn't buy it at first.

00:14:20.165 --> 00:14:22.498
And then, I'll never forget.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:25.265
We formed a relationship,

00:14:25.265 --> 00:14:27.913
and we used to talk and chop it up.

00:14:27.913 --> 00:14:30.081
Chop it up is like converse.

00:14:30.081 --> 00:14:30.934
- Thank you.

00:14:30.934 --> 00:14:32.883
I kind of figured that. (laughing)

00:14:32.883 --> 00:14:35.135
But thanks for the translation.

00:14:35.135 --> 00:14:36.580
Thank you, Drake.

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:40.428
- (laughing) And so we would
talk, and he called me one day.

00:14:40.428 --> 00:14:43.706
I was in the barber shop
getting my hair cut.

00:14:43.706 --> 00:14:46.084
But he called me from his number.

00:14:46.084 --> 00:14:46.964
But it was like (imitates phone ringing).

00:14:46.964 --> 00:14:48.458
And the phone rang, and I picked it up.

00:14:48.458 --> 00:14:49.612
And it was like, "Yo."

00:14:49.612 --> 00:14:51.911
And I was like, you
probably know that voice.

00:14:51.911 --> 00:14:54.071
I was like hello?

00:14:54.071 --> 00:14:55.143
It was like, "Yo, what's up?"

00:14:55.143 --> 00:14:57.879
I was like this doesn't
sound like my friend.

00:14:57.879 --> 00:14:59.662
And he's like, "Yo,
what's up, it's Weezy."

00:14:59.662 --> 00:15:01.995
And it ended up being Wayne.

00:15:02.936 --> 00:15:05.874
And he was like I'm starting
this thing called Young Money

00:15:05.874 --> 00:15:07.174
and I'd really love for
you to be a part of it.

00:15:07.174 --> 00:15:09.978
So I want to fly you out
to Houston and meet you.

00:15:09.978 --> 00:15:13.423
And he did just that the day after.

00:15:13.423 --> 00:15:14.701
And that formed our relationship.

00:15:14.701 --> 00:15:18.463
And I was like this quiet
kid in the corner of the bus

00:15:18.463 --> 00:15:20.409
while everything was going on around me.

00:15:20.409 --> 00:15:22.520
Tha Carter III was just,
I think it was like

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:24.844
maybe two or three weeks
away from coming out

00:15:24.844 --> 00:15:27.353
and what a time, what a time.

00:15:27.353 --> 00:15:29.248
- What kind of advice did he give you

00:15:29.248 --> 00:15:30.485
or how did he help you

00:15:30.485 --> 00:15:33.483
kind of take your music to the next step?

00:15:33.483 --> 00:15:35.884
- The greatest advice
Wayne has ever given me,

00:15:35.884 --> 00:15:37.463
and it's a constant.

00:15:37.463 --> 00:15:40.640
It's less of advice and
more of a constant reminder

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:43.649
which I love him so much
for saying this to me,

00:15:43.649 --> 00:15:47.164
is he's always just like
man, please be yourself.

00:15:47.164 --> 00:15:50.993
Please don't ever try and
be me or anybody else.

00:15:50.993 --> 00:15:53.076
Don't ever go get tattoos.

00:15:53.076 --> 00:15:56.300
You don't have to dress any different.

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:59.967
Because from the day
Wayne met me until now,

00:16:01.245 --> 00:16:03.158
I haven't changed anything about myself.

00:16:03.158 --> 00:16:06.925
He met me, and he really
liked the kid that he met.

00:16:06.925 --> 00:16:08.014
- How old were you then?

00:16:08.014 --> 00:16:09.311
How old were you, Drake, when you met him?

00:16:09.311 --> 00:16:11.614
- That was about, I'd say
it was like two years ago?

00:16:11.614 --> 00:16:13.205
- Yeah, two or three,
when that album came out.

00:16:13.205 --> 00:16:15.243
Yeah.
- Yep, two years ago.

00:16:15.243 --> 00:16:16.915
And he was like don't stop smiling either.

00:16:16.915 --> 00:16:18.569
Don't try and get mean or aggressive.

00:16:18.569 --> 00:16:19.967
He's like just be you, man.

00:16:19.967 --> 00:16:23.446
Just be you and rap about
life and women and family

00:16:23.446 --> 00:16:24.957
and just love life and be happy.

00:16:24.957 --> 00:16:25.790
Be that guy.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:26.956
Be the guy that I could never be,

00:16:26.956 --> 00:16:28.129
because he can't be that guy.

00:16:28.129 --> 00:16:30.045
Because he has tattoos all over his face,

00:16:30.045 --> 00:16:31.126
then he has dreads,

00:16:31.126 --> 00:16:32.630
and he has diamonds in his mouth,

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:33.996
and he's a completely different person.

